pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">956975</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="supported-by"><p>This study was supported by Grant No. <award-id>R13-2002-028-0100-0</award-id> from <funding-source>Basic Research Program of the Korean Science and Engineering Foundation (KOSEF)</funding-source> to the Chronic Disease Research Center at Keimyung University.</p></fn><fn fn-type="other"><p>This study is based in part on a study first reported in the Korean J Pediatr 2005;48:991-7.</p></fn></fn-group></back><floats-group><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Clinical data and indexes of suspicion of typical cow's milk protein-induced enterocolitis (CMPIE) compared with infection and non-infection group</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-993-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>By ANOVA (analysis of variance); <sup>&#x02020;</sup><italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05 (vs. CMPIE group) by Turkey's test for all pairwise comparisons; <sup>&#x02021;</sup>No.=62; <sup>&#x000a7;</sup><italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05 (vs. Infection group) by Turkey's test for all pairwise comparisons; <sup>&#x02016;</sup>No.=14; <sup>&#x000b6;</sup>by Fisher's exact test.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>